{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1454361-deviant-questions-about-symbiotes","id":1454361,"title":"(Deviant) Questions about symbiotes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-06T10:26:29-07:00","id":1454361,"title":"(Deviant) Questions about symbiotes","content":"Hello, I hope you help me with some questions about the Symbiote Form:<br /> <br /> 1) The character and the symbiote can communicate each other?<br /> <br /> 2) Also the two halves can willingly switch on control, or it's always a conflictual event?<br /> <br /> 3) Everything can count as symbiote?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T15:51:41-07:00","id":1454386,"title":"","content":"1) The symbiote can communicate with the host character. What form this takes is up to the individual character concept, ranging the full spectrum from &quot;the symbiote is not sapient and feels only a set of instincts and simple desires, which the host can feel fighting against or contributing to their actions as appropriate&quot; to &quot;the symbiote is fully sapient, speaks English fluently, and is very opinionated and chatty, though it is restricted to having telepathic conversations with you inside your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) The Symbiote Form represents having a &quot;passenger&quot; symbiote that can make the actions the host takes easier or harder, but which is not able to outright take control and force the host to do anything. The host has full control over whether they do something the symbiote wants or not, and the symbiote is only able to distract the host or split his attention.<br /> <br /> Characters who are fused with another intelligence that <i>can</i> take control, leaving essentially two people to war over control over one body, can be made, but instead of using the Symbiote Form, these characters should be represented with the Alternate Persona Scar. An Alternate Persona normally wrests temporary control from the host character, but modifying it with Deviations like Invoked, Partner, and Perfect Recall can make for two intelligences cooperating and voluntarily sharing time within the body.<br /> <br /> 3) It doesn't matter what kind of entity or origin a Symbiote (or for that matter an Alternate Persona) comes from, just what form it takes. In the case of the Symbiote Form, it means there's something inside you that has its own separate desires from yours, making you better at doing things it wants done and worse at doing things it wants to avoid. In the case of Alternate Persona, it means there's another intelligence inside you that can temporarily take control over your body, leaving you submerged and helpless for the duration.<br /> <br /> All of that can mean a split personality formed by a psychotic break, a possessing spirit fused to your soul, a parasitic fungus that interferes with brain activity, an artificial intelligence cybernetically wired to your nervous system, a scientifically freakish second brain of some kind, whatever fits.<br /> <br /> Deviants are a thousand different kinds of monster. The only thing consistent across all of them is their need for someone to cling to and someone to hate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T00:07:41-07:00","id":1454430,"title":"","content":"Thank you, your reply is really useful!<br /> <br /> Anyway in my character concept the symbiote is a micrichip into his brain which due to a bug became a sentient AI, and it can even manifest to the deviant in the form of an allucination (more or less like Morgan Dexter's dad). Do you think it can work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T08:19:57-07:00","id":1454451,"title":"","content":"Sounds A-OK to me, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}